Description: stop the device thread cooperatively instead of kill_thread
 The destructor reaped the device message-loop thread with kill_thread(),
 which on VOS kills the whole team instead of one thread. Stop() already
 hands the loop its QUIT_COMMAND through the port and waits for it to be
 consumed; send that if the port is still open, then wait_for_thread()
 the thread.
Author: VitruvianOS Packagers <maintainers@v-os.dev>
Forwarded: no
Origin: https://github.com/HaikuArchives/KeyCursor
--- a/src/KeyCursorDevice.cpp
+++ b/src/KeyCursorDevice.cpp
@@ -66,10 +66,14 @@
 
 KeyCursorDevice::~KeyCursorDevice()
 {
-	if (fThreadID != -1) {
-		// just in case.
-		kill_thread(fThreadID);
-	}
+	// Cooperative stop: kill_thread() would take the whole team on VOS.
+	// Stop() already hands the loop its QUIT_COMMAND through the port;
+	// send that if the port is still open, then reap the thread.
+	thread_id tid = fThreadID;
+	if (fPortID > 0)
+		Stop(NULL, NULL);
+	if (tid != -1)
+		wait_for_thread(tid, NULL);
 }
 
 
